  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Frogs go through 4 stages in their lifecycle, going through metamorphosis
    to reach full maturity. It starts with frogspawn, a big clump of eggs with a
    jelly like coating to keep the eggs moist and bind them together for protection.
    These eggs hatch into tadpoles with legs who swim around in fresh water as they
    mature. Their tails slowly shrink and skin forms over the gills. These tadpoles
    metamorphose into froglets which resemble a mix of the tadpole appearance and
    the fully developed frog. Then finally the frogs reach full maturity when they
    have fully developed lungs and can breathe above water
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
