      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'A vast number of shark species are in critial danger due to overfishing,
    bycatch, habitat degredation and having their fins cut off to make shark fin
    soup.  Of the 1,199 species assessed, 121 are classed as Endangered, 90 as Critically
    Endangered and 180 as Vulnerable. Sharks are very slow to reproduce and take
    a long time to reach sexual maturity so it makes it difficult for their populations
    to come back after declining. It is important that we protect these fascinating
    creatures to ensure the stability of the ecosystems they live in. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
