  m_text: Shark anatomy varies greatly between each species. Some shark such as the
    great white sharks (far right) do not have any muscles around their gills meaning
    that to survive they have to keep swimming endlessly to pump water through their
    gills. Other sharks like the wobbegong do have muscles around their gills and
    even sit on the ocean floor hunting for prey!
